<title>USA: TABLE - Rubbermaid Inc Q2 net increases.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Rubbermaid Inc Q2 net increases.</headline>
<dateline>WOOSTER, Ohio 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended</p>
<p>					Jun 30, 1997	Jun 30, 1996</p>
<p>NET EARNINGS PER</p>
<p>   COMMON SHARE			$     0.31	 $     0.30</p>
<p> Net sales				  640,379	    572,989</p>
<p> Cost of sales			    466,364	    389,127</p>
<p> Net earnings				46,595	     44,750</p>
<p>						     Six Months Ended</p>
<p>					Jun 30, 1997	Jun 30, 1996</p>
<p>NET EARNINGS PER</p>
<p>   COMMON SHARE			$     0.54	 $     0.57</p>
<p> Net Sales				1,242,067	  1,106,274</p>
<p> Net earnings				80,620	     86,427</p>
<p>(Dollars in thousands except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE:  The company reported average shares outstanding of 149,918,851 and 150,348,835 for the respective 1997 and 1996 three-month periods and 149,906,300 and 152,241,168 for the respective six-month periods.</p>
<p>Net income for 1997 Q2 includes an after-tax gain of $0.53 per share on the recent divestiture of the company's Office Products business to Newell Co, as well as a previously announced charge of $0.47 per share after taxes related to certain intangible assets associated with the integration of acquisitions and revised realignment cost.</p>
</text>
